REMark
REMark Sample BOOT file for use with ELVIS
REMark ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
:
REMark  You do not HAVE to use a BOOT file to run ELVIS.  There are,
REMark  however, options you can set in a BOOT file to tailor ELVIS
REMark  to your system.   This file (while useable as it stands)
REMark  is merely a model.  You will probably want to modify it to
REMark  suit your own system and preferences
REMark
REMark  Probably more useful is to add relevant entries to your normal
REMark  BOOT file.   You will then be able to EXEC ELVIS at any time.
:
MODE 4   :                        REMark set monitor mode (4 colour)
TK2_EXT  :                        REMark activate Toolkit 2
PROG_USE "Flp1_" :                REMark  Set directory for program files
DATA_USE "Flp2_" :                REMark  Set directory for data files
:
LRESPR  PROGD$ & "env_bin" :      REMark  Load C68 environment variable support
:
REMark   Environment variables  - set these to suit your own style of working
:
SETENV "TERM=qdos" :              REMark Terminal type in TERMINFO file
SETENV "TERMINFO=flp1_terminfo" : REMark Path for finding TERMINFO_QDOS file
SETENV "TEMP=ram1_" :             REMark  temporary directory
SETENV "TMP=ram1_" :              REMark  (alternative for some programs)
:
EXEC "Elvis" :                    REMark  ...finally load Elvis program
:
PRINT #0,"Type CTRL-C to switch to and from ELVIS."
PRINT #0,"CTRL-L refreshes the screen when in ELVIS."
